            "learn": {
                "paragraphs": [
                    "**1. Multiplication Principle:** If an event can occur in $m$ ways, and another event can occur in $n$ ways, then the total number of ways the two events can occur **simultaneously** is $m \\times n$.",
                    "**2. Addition Principle:** If an event can occur in $m$ ways OR $n$ ways (mutually exclusive), the total ways is $m + n$.",
                    "**3. Tree Diagram:** A visual way to represent these branching choices."
                ],
                "formulas": [
                    {
                        "rule": "Multiplication Rule",
                        "formula": "\\text{Total} = m_1 \\times m_2 \\times m_3 \\dots",
